  body: "# CA temporary breaks in care\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured guidance provides conditional
    treatment of temporary breaks as weeks satisfying the caring condition, with prior-care and hospital-treatment
    requirements.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nRead DMG 60045–60050 across pages 7–8, including Memo 06/20, time
    limits and continued qualifying-benefit payment. This is not an automatic holiday or hospital entitlement. The
    shorter payment list in 60050 and expanded 60033 require review.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 60045, PDF
    page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=7).\n-
    [DMG 60047, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=8).\n\
    - [DMG 60050, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=8).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 60, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 60, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=8).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch60`:
    PDF `ab9fed933c167b4ac18039204c3853c425731ffb4239022a11b41884caaee22a`; extracted pages `bc5925c0d434fbc4bec575bea2e1e2dbd020b014497ab156973054e80e326f2f`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.596227Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0fdcbb5e95ca5017ed9da/dmg-Chap-60.pdf#page=7
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/ca-qualifying-disability-payment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The hospital passage makes continuing payment of the qualifying disability benefit relevant to
      CA.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0008
      quote: "60050 Where the reason for the temporary break in care is because the severely disabled person is
        in\nhospital, entitlement to CA will depend on the continuing payment of\n\n\n1. AA or\n\n\n2. the care
        component of DLA at the highest or middle rate or\n\n\n3. CAA.\n\n\nIf payment of these benefits ends there
        can be no entitlement to CA 1. The severely disabled person in\neffect is not classed as severely disabled
        due to the fact that the benefit they are entitled to is no longer\npayable after a prescribed period of
        time in hospital. See DMG 60033 for meaning of severely disabled\nperson.\n\n\n                        \
        \                                                           1 SS CB Act 1992, s 70(2)\n\n\n\nGainful employment"
      locator: DMG 60050
